TimeFrameSigil::checkAction
├── given an unsatisfiable window
│   └── it can never reach checkAction — it is rejected at init (UnsatisfiableWindow)
├── given a configured satisfiable window [validAfter, validUntil]
│   ├── when block.timestamp is strictly inside the window
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
│   ├── when block.timestamp == validAfter (lower bound inclusive)
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
│   ├── when block.timestamp == validUntil (upper bound inclusive)
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
│   ├── when block.timestamp < validAfter
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
│   └── when block.timestamp > validUntil
│       └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given validUntil == 0 (no upper bound)
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS arbitrarily far in the future
├── given validAfter == 0 (no lower bound)
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS from the earliest timestamp
├── given the open (0, 0) window
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS at any timestamp
├── given an uninitialized config
│   └── it should read as the open (0, 0) window and return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
├── it should read NO calldata (empty data in-window succeeds)
├── it should enforce NO value cap (non-zero value in-window succeeds)
└── fuzz: success EXACTLY equals the window-membership predicate over satisfiable windows
